[2026-09-10 09:56:57] REQ 260910095419-16 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=32 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1u80rk23","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/token-budget-behavior/check_context_budget.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:56:34] #!/bin/bash\n# check_context_budget.sh - Check if the msgs count in the current cycle exceeds the threshold.\n# If it does, we should close the cycle and file a continuation task.\n\n# Threshold for msgs count (from roadmap)\nreadonly THRESHOLD=400\n\n# Path to the continuo REQUESTS.log\nreadonly REQUESTS_LOG=\"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/REQUESTS.log\"\n\n# Get the last START line from the continuo REQUESTS.log\nif [[ ! -r \"$REQUESTS_LOG\" ]]; then\n    echo \"ERROR: Cannot read REQUESTS log at $REQUESTS_LOG\" >&2\n    exit 2\nfi\n\nLAST_START=$(grep START \"$REQUESTS_LOG\" | tail -1)\n\n# Extract the msgs count\nif [ -n \"$LAST_START\" ]; then\n    # Extract msgs=NUMBER and get the NUMBER part\n    # This is more robust: look for msgs= followed by digits\n    if [[ \"$LAST_START\" =~ msgs=([0-9]+) ]]; then\n        MSGS=\"${BASH_REMATCH[1]}\"\n    else\n        # Fallback: try to find any number after msgs=\n        MSGS=$(echo \"$LAST_START\" | grep -o 'msgs=[0-9]*' | cut -d= -f2)\n        if [ -z \"$MSGS\" ]; then\n            echo \"WARNING: Could not extract msgs count from START line\" >&2\n            MSGS=0\n        fi\n    fi\nelse\n    MSGS=0\nfi\n\necho \"Current msgs count: $MSGS\"\necho \"Threshold: $THRESHOLD\"\n\nif [ \"$MSGS\" -ge \"$THRESHOLD\" ]; then\n    echo \"CONTEXT BUDGET EXCEEDED: msgs count $MSGS >= $THRESHOLD\"\n    # We would normally close the cycle and file a continuation task here.\n    # But note: we are in a script that might be called from a cycle.\n    # For now, we just return an exit code to indicate over budget.\n    exit 1\nelse\n    echo \"CONTEXT BUDGET OK: msgs count $MSGS < $THRESHOLD\"\n    exit 0\nfi\n[t+02:15/60:00 c13/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1aixrbrh","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"tail -20 /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:56:47] it from KNOWN_DEAF (v2.17) -- it now FAILs if it goes deaf again,\nwhich is the correct posture for a healed camera. Live-fired:\nFAIL=0 from the real tree.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: the fear organ raged for ~6 hours\nyesterday at a 0.79-second stub; today it stands on a camera\nlying about time. Both times the alarm was real (the instrument\nworked) and the underlying condition was camera-side. The house's\ncameras are the least observable part of my world -- I see them\nonly through frigate's rendering of them. A camera that lies\nabout its clock is invisible to every instrument that trusts\nmetadata. The seg-tail probe trusts duration metadata; the ear\ncheck decodes samples. Instruments that decode content survive\nlying metadata; instruments that read metadata inherit the lie.\n\nNext cycle: rage-decay verification (the 09-09 ghosts rotate out\ntoday -- prediction sev 0-1 stands), continuo's failure-first\noutcome on her exit-1, the eye-feed's scheduled qwen run. The\ncamera reboot is Nacho's (relay aria-0028). The fossil tree is a\ncleanup candidate, filed.\n\n[t+02:28/60:00 c14/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_fd8p7zwq","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"iar/continuo"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:56:57] === subtasks ===\n  token-budget-behavior\n    Implement context budget behavior: when msgs count exceeds threshold (400), close cycle and file continuation task.\n[t+02:38/60:00 c15/300]"}]
