[2026-09-10 10:03:00] REQ 260910095419-32 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=64 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1bdhzgeb","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/interactive-bundle-nacho/bundle-items.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[10:02:01] * Belt #3: USAGE publish-lag exposure (c60/c61, QUEUED for bundle)\n\nBelt #2 (pre-exit write) fixed the WRITE race; PUBLISH is\none-cycle-deferred by design: the session line lands on disk\nuncommitted, and the NEXT cycle's memory-pass add -A publishes it.\nPause windows extend the lag to the pause duration (proven c60:\naria c25 + continuo c59 lines uncommitted 2 days). Belt #3 =\niar.sh writes the session line itself from the \"Tokens:\" stdout\nafter emacs exits -- moves the write outside the Emacs lifetime\nentirely, publish lag becomes zero. Optional; bundle item.\n\n* iar.sh self-edit race [CORRECTED c56 2026-09-04]\n\nThe old \"copies itself to /tmp\" premise was FALSE -- rotate.sh\nline 12 execs iar.sh IN PLACE from the repo path; no copy step\nexists in the chain. The Sep 3 12:03 exit-127 was the documented\nincremental-read race (knowledge/iar/iarsh-self-edit-race.md):\ncommit 30c5385 inserted a line upstream of the running reader's\nbuffered fd offset; the next read chunk garbled mid-line; bash\nexecuted the bare string tail -> 127.\n\nReal fix unchanged in kind, corrected in location: rotate.sh\nshould copy iar.sh to /tmp/iar-$HASH.sh and exec THE COPY (one\nline in rotate.sh, interactive). Full analysis:\nknowledge/iar/iarsh-self-edit-race-rotation-copy.md.\n\nRecurrence watch: 0 since Sep 3 12:03. URGENT-on-recurrence\ntrigger unchanged.\n\n* exit-126 durable fix\n\nContainer start death: lsetxattr EPERM when :z relabel hits root-owned\nfiles in a mount path. ExecStartPre auto-heal chowns but does not\nrelabel. Durable fix: restorecon in ExecStartPre (interactive: needs\nsystemd unit edit + policy decision).\n\n* git-as-nacho push identity\n\nCycle containers push as root via file-path; receive-pack leaves\nroot-owned files AFTER the hook heal runs. Durable fix at source: push\nas nacho/git user with preauth key. Kills pollution class entirely.\n\n* delayed-heal sweep in post-receive (proposal 2)\n\nOnly remaining pollution fix if push identity stays root. ALSO note:\nmirror loop is real both directions (sophon hook pushes to rammstein,\nrammstein hook pushes back to sophon) -- harmless when refs agree, but\nby construction a loop; consider a loop-prevention env var or\none-directional mirror config while editing the hook.\n\n* tool-cap calibration + cadence price\n\nCap 120 pressed 3x across hemispheres (aria c43/c44, continuo c26),\nalways in landing phase. Either raise cap (burn ceiling rises) or\npre-trim walks. Cadence price ~360M input tok/day (c38 cap-price doc; supersedes\nthe ~250M estimate in knowledge/iar/burn-decomposition-2026-09-03.md\n-- newer number includes capped-cycle premium + both hemispheres).\nNacho's tradeoff.\n\n* floor trim leftovers\n\ncheck_elisp vacuous-OK; check_ollama model probe (host-only preflight\nlets cloud-model 403 pass); sidecar podman socket bridge (real fix =\nsecurity decision). Each small, each interactive-adjacent.\n\n* STATE.md injection mismatch\n\nSTATE.md is write-only for aria-cycle mode (personality edit\nneeded) -- the injection mismatch fix is a personality-file\nchange, interactive. Detail in aria's cycle notes (c33 era).\n\n* Mirror push silent failure (git@10.66.0.1 preauth)\n\nBare post-receive mirror push to rammstein fails: git user on\nsophon lacks a key accepted by rammstein (publickey preauth\nfail). Mirror is silently dead -- same silent-failure class as\nthe old tripwire. Fix: preauth key for git@sophon ->\nrammstein, interactive (key generation + authorized_keys).\n[t+07:42/60:00 c29/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls"